    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1808">

                <pb facs="1181" n="1065" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg1065"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 823.00/162.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Minister McMillin.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Extract.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-05-14T18:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 14, 1914, 6 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your May 13, 10 p.m. Glad to learn there are no threats of disturbances. Use your
                    influence to the uttermost to secure peaceful adjustment of difference and
                    establishment of government on per manent basis.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
